s point to a solid Republican hold: the state leans heavily Republican, Jackley won his primary and outraised Gronli by roughly five to one, and markets give Gronli only about a 4% chance. The lone Democratic-sponsored poll showing a 4-point race is an outlier against this backdrop, so the expected margin stays near fourteen points Republican.", "watch": "A shift in the national environment toward Democrats, or additional independent polling confirming a single-digit race, would narrow this forecast.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Open seat: Dusty Johnson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Dakota's at-large House seat is open this cycle as Dusty Johnson leaves to run for governor. Republican Marty Jackley, a former attorney general who won a contested primary, faces Democrat Nikki Gronli, a party activist with limited fundraising. The district's strong Republican lean makes this seat difficult for any Democrat to carry.\n\nJackley holds a large financial edge, with more than $1 million on hand compared with Gronli's roughly $110,000, and no significant outside spending has targeted the race. A late Democratic-sponsored poll showed a surprisingly close 4-point contest, but prediction markets still price Jackley as a heavy favorite. The forecast expects a Republican win by a comfortable, though not overwhelming, margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -15.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0239, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01